      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Acute obstruction of the left anterior descending coronary artery is generally presented electrocardiographically as isolated anterior or combined anterior and inferior ST-elevation myocardial infarction. We described an isolated inferolateral ST-elevation myocardial infarction due to acute occlusion of the distal left anterior descending coronary artery."},
